        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://tallapoosaga.gov/about/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A historic marker titled “Seven Chestnuts” commemorates Creek council meetings held under seven chestnut trees in Tallapoosa.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tallapoosa%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1887 the Columbus Enquirer‑Sun called Tallapoosa “a Georgia town with a great future” thanks to mineral resources and the Tallapoosa Land, Mineral, and Mining Company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://tallapoosaga.gov/about/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Georgia‑Pacific Railroad, built in 1882, spurred Tallapoosa’s growth when the Georgia‑Alabama Investment and Development Co. planned a new city along its tracks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.georgiahistory.com/ghmi_marker_updated/historic-tallapoosa/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Every New Year’s Eve, Tallapoosa hosts one of Georgia’s largest Possum Drop celebrations, a quirky tradition that draws crowds from across the state.",
